ll betting: Should you still bet on Indiana to make the CFP?","description":"The Hoosiers dropped to No. 14 in the latest CPF rankings, but are they still a good bet to make the playoff?","published":"2026-11-25T04:16:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50588403/2026-college-football-playoff-cfp-indiana-hoosiers","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 Anger Index: Indiana dropped how many spots?!","description":"Ranking the teams that should be most upset with the latest CFP rankings.","published":"2026-11-25T03:26:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50582371/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the College Football Playoff bubble after committee's fourth ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-25T03:24:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575185/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-fourth-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Why UTEP-NIU is 2026's most unglamorous Game of the Century","description":"The Week 13 game will mark the first time since at least 2000 that two teams that are winless against FBS opponents will meet in their final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-25T01:19:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50587546/utep-niu-college-football-game-century","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana falls from 12-team field in 4th CFP rankings; Horns, Vols leap Bama","description":"Defending champ Indiana fell six spots to No. 14, while Alabama was leaped by Texas and Tennessee and fell out of the top five in the latest CFP rankings Tuesday night.","published":"2026-11-25T07:42:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50588082/indiana-top-12-cfp-rankings-texas-tennessee-leap-alabama","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the move? CFP committee's fourth top 25 and bracket of 2026","description":"A look at the new bracket based on the College Football Playoff committee's fourth set of rankings.","published":"2026-11-25T02:02:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584328/cfp-2026-fourth-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU asks judge to throw out SEC's 'unwarranted' suit against Tigers","description":"LSU is asking a federal judge to dismiss the SEC's lawsuit against the Tigers, arguing that many of the plaintiffs in the case are protected by sovereign immunity as state officials and that the league doesn't have jurisdiction.","published":"2026-11-25T05:10:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50588015/lsu-asks-judge-throw-sec-unwarranted-suit-tigers","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Stanford quarterback Davis Warren returning in 2027","description":"Davis Warren has agreed to return to the Cardinal for his final year of eligibility, sources said.","published":"2026-11-25T01:32:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50588012/stanford-quarterback-davis-warren-returning-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wyoming's Jay Sawvel gets self-imposed 1-game ban over tampering violations","description":"Wyoming coach Jay Sawvel will serve a one-game suspension Saturday as part of the school's self-imposed penalties for impermissible contacting of players.","published":"2026-11-25T00:01:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50586972/wyoming-coach-jay-sawvel-gets-self-imposed-1-game-suspension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5077638/bray-hubbard","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bray_Hubbard"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Bray Hubbard","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bray_Hubbard","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:43Z","intro":"Brayson \"Bray\" Hubbard (born February 14, 2005) is an American college football safety for the Alabama Crimson Tide.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Hubbard was born in Ocean Springs, Mississippi and attended Ocean Springs High School. He was rated as a three-star recruit and committed to play college football for the Alabama Crimson Tide over offers from FAU, Mississippi State, Navy, Tulane, and Southern Miss."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman in 2023, Hubbard appeared in nine games for Alabama, notching one tackle. In week 8 of the 2024 season, he notched nine tackles in a 24–17 loss to Tennessee, after replacing injured starter Keon Sabb. Heading into week 9, Hubbard was named the team's starting safety due to Sabb's injury. In his first career start, he totaled seven tackles and an interception in a win over Missouri. Hubbard went viral for jogging during a play that resulted in a touchdown versus Florida State in 2025."}]}}